  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 255 PM EDT Sat Oct 24 2026\n\nAnother pleasant Fall day has played out across the region with \nmostly sunny skies and temperatures in the 60s and low 70s. Guidance \nremains in agreement with the strength and positioning of our upper \nlevel ridge over the Ohio Valley region through mid-week. This \nfeature will continue to influence our weather pattern for much of \nthe next 7 days. The ridge axis will gradually shift east over the \nnext few days while incoming shortwave trough over the Great Lake \nregion will successfully weaken the ridge mid-week. Latest model \ntrends keep us dry through next Friday with rain chances beginning \nnext Sunday. Models have gradually slowed down the incoming system \nfor next weekend that it now appears that Halloween should remain \ndry. This is great news for those of us excited for the holiday. \n\nPersistence type weather forecast with lows in the 40s with non-zero \nchance of patchy fog development while daytime highs are in the \nupper 60s and lower 70s with mostly sunny skies. This pattern will \nsupport ample mixing and lower afternoon relative humidity values, \nbut light winds should limit any meaningful fire weather concerns \nfor now.",
